  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "AI-Native Organizations",
      "items": [
        "Hub: AI-Native Company. Mechanism: Organizational Legibility feeds a Self-Improving AI Loop, which fills a Company Brain; Fix the Principle keeps the loop learning.",
        "Around it: Role Archetypes, Founder as Orchestrator, Everyone Ships, Prototype/Dogfood/Productionize, Build for Rebuilding, Startup Lifecycle.",
        "Open: one intelligence layer or a mesh of sources of truth (Company Brain's contested claim)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "AI-Native Software Engineering",
      "items": [
        "Hub: Verification Bottleneck; every other page is a consequence of building collapsing. Advisory and Deterministic Controls says which rules hold; Tiered Autonomy says how much an agent earns; AI-Native SDLC rebuilds the lifecycle around committed artifacts.",
        "Open: Just-in-Time Planning's contested claim that prototypes replace design docs, against the SDLC's enforced plan.md."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "The Knowledge Layer",
      "items": [
        "Hub: Three-Layer Architecture. Thesis: Why LLM Wikis Beat RAG. Write path: Ingest Workflow. Comparators each test one piece: Skill Evolution (WikiSkill), Belief Ledger (gbrain), Provenance Tags (obsidian-wiki, OpenWiki), Unattended Agent State (Anthropic).",
        "Compounding has exactly one controlled measurement (WikiSkill: 63.7% vs 48.7%). Fractal Federation and Subtractive Onboarding describe the template and carry no claims."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Bridges between clusters",
      "items": [
        "Company Brain is the org-side name for what Three-Layer Architecture builds for one domain.",
        "A Self-Improving AI Loop needs the verification the engineering cluster describes before it runs unattended.",
        "Advisory and Deterministic Controls is the same advise-or-enforce split that Ingest Workflow and lint make in this KB."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Sourcing",
      "items": [
        "The organizations and engineering clusters share most sources, so agreement between them is one vendor's view twice. Outside voices: two YC talks and one consultant's feature list.",
        "Most supported claims mean no source has contested them yet. What would move the map most: a non-vendor account of an AI-native org at scale, and a second controlled study of a compiled wiki."
      ]
    }
  ]
